red or choose to sell their holdings and holders of the Green Notes, Social Notes and/or Sustainability Notes may receive less than their initial investment in selling their Green Notes, Social Notes and/or Sustainability Notes before the final redemption of the Notes. Risks related to Shared Coupon Notes In accordance with Condition 5(l) and if “Shared Coupon Notes” is specified as “Applicable” in the applicable Final Terms, the Issuer shall deduct the relevant Shared Amount(s) from the amounts due to the Noteholder under the Notes, provided that the Shared Amount Percentage may be deducted from the relevant Rate of Interest or the Margin before calculating the relevant interest amount to pay, as specified in the applicable Final Terms. Such Shared Amount(s) will then be paid on the Shared Amount Payment Date(s) to the Non-Profit Organisation(s) on behalf of the Noteholders to fund the Project(s), unless a Shared Amount Stop Event or an Early Redemption Termination Event occurs prior to any such Shared Amount Payment Date(s). Therefore, the return on Shared Coupon Notes will likely be lower than the return on a standard debt security of comparable maturity. The return that a Noteholder will receive on the Shared Coupon Notes may be less than the return such Noteholder could earn on other investments. Although the Issuer is under no obligation to purchase Notes at any time from Noteholders, it may elect to do so pursuant to, and subject to the conditions set out in, Condition 6(k)(i). In such case, the repurchase price, whether conditional or hypothetical, proposed by the Issuer may be reduced by an amount equal to the aggregate Shared Amounts yet to be paid until (and including) the Maturity Date had the Notes not been so purchased and cancelled, unless a Shared Amount Stop Event has occurred. This could negatively affect the value of the Shared Coupon Notes and result in investors losing all or a portion of their initial investment, if they consent to sell their N