r their determination but in no event later than the fourth Business Day thereafter. The amount of interest payable per Specified Denomination and Interest Payment Date so published may subsequently be amended (or appropriate alternative arrangements made by way of adjustment) without notice in the event of an extension or shortening of the Interest Period. If the Notes become due and payable under Condition 9, the accrued interest per Specified Denomination shall nevertheless continue to be calculated as previously by the Calculation Agent in accordance with this provision but no publication of the amount of interest payable per Specified Denomination so calculated need be made. Interest shall be calculated in respect of any period by applying the Rate of Interest to the Specified Denomination, multiplying such product by the actual number of days in the relevant Interest Period or, as applicable, other period concerned and dividing it by 365, and rounding the resultant figure to the nearest Renminbi sub-unit, half of any such sub-unit being rounded upwards or otherwise in accordance with applicable market convention. (l) Shared Coupon Notes (only applicable to Senior Preferred Notes having a denomination of at least €100,000): (i) Shared Coupon Notes If “Shared Coupon Notes” is specified as “Applicable” in the applicable Final Terms, the Issuer shall deduct the relevant Shared Amount(s) from the Interest Amount due to the Noteholder under the Notes on the relevant Interest Payment Date, provided that the relevant Shared Amount Percentage may be deducted from the relevant Rate of Interest or the Margin before calculating the relevant interest amount, as specified in the applicable Final Terms. Such Shared Amount(s) will then be paid by the Issuer on the Shared Amount Payment Date(s) to the Non-Profit Organisation(s) on behalf of the Noteholders to fund the Project(s), unless a Shared Amount Stop Event or an Early Redemption Termination Event occurs prior to any such Shared Amount Payment Date(s). In accordance with the applicable Undertaking Agreement, the Non-Profit Organisation is required to provide the Issuer with a certificate (a “NPO Certificate”) within a maximum of 60 days following the relevant Shared Amount Payment Date or any such other period as may be set forth in the applicable Undertaking Agreement (the “NPO Certificate Cut-off Date”). The NPO Certificate will confirm that the Non-Profit Organisation (i) has received the Shared Amount from the Issuer, (ii) has used or intends to use the Shared Amount to fund the Project(s) in accordance with the Undertaking Agreement, and (iii) complies with applicable laws and regulations. The Issuer shall notify the Noteholders of the occurrence of a Shared Amount Stop Event in accordance with Condition 16 as soon as reasonably practicable thereafter, but in any event no later than 45 days after the occurrence of the Shared Amount Stop Event. 3214583142 121 In the event a Shared Amount Stop Event or an Early Redemption Termination Event occurs, the Issuer shall forthwith cease to deduct the Shared Amount and the Noteholders shall be entitled to the full Interest Amount on each subsequent Interest Payment Date. The Shared Amount will be paid on behalf of the Noteholders to the Non-Profit Organisation by the Issuer (or the Paying Agent acting on behalf of, and instructed by, the Issuer) to make such payment. For the avoidance of doubt, no delay, absence or disruption in the payment of the Shared Amount to the Non- Profit Organisation by the Issuer (or the Paying Agent acting on behalf of, and instructed by, the Issuer) to make such payment, shall constitute an event of default for the purposes hereof or otherwise. The Issuer shall not be held liable to the Noteholders or the Non-Profit Organisation for any loss, damage, cost, expense or liability arising from or in connection with the failure or negligence of the Paying Agent to perform its obligations in relation to the payment of the Shared Amount, and neither the Noteholders nor the Non-Profit Organisation shall have any recourse to the Issuer in respect of such payment. The Shared Amount will represent a fraction of the Interest Amount due to the Noteholders under the Notes. As a result, the Shared Amount cannot exceed the Interest Amount in accordance with this Condition. (ii) Acknowledgments by Noteholders By acquiring any Shared Coupon Note, each Noteholder acknowledges, accepts and agrees, notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Conditions, that: (A) it will not be entitled to receive any Shared Amount in respect of the Shared Coupon Notes, unless a Shared Amount Stop Event or an Early Redemption Termination Event has occurred; (B) whether “Tax Certificate” is specified as “Applicable” or “Not Applicable” in the applicable Final Terms, the Issuer will not and has no obligation or responsibility to issue, deliver or obtain any Tax Certificate for the Noteholders. The Issuer cannot be held liable if the Non-Profit Organisation fails to deliver a Tax Certificate and such failure shall not in any way constitute a default under the Notes or otherwise. Furthermore, the Noteholders shall have no recourse against the Issuer in respect of any Tax Certificate or any tax benefit or relief arising (or not arising) from the payment of the Shared Amount(s). If “Tax Certificate” is specified as “Not Applicable” in the applicable Final Terms, neither the Non-Profit Organisation nor the Issuer will provide the Noteholders with any Tax Certificate, and in such case, each and any Noteholder (whether it is an initial Noteholder or a person or entity which becomes a Noteholder for any reason) acknowledges that they will not be entitled to any tax credit or deduction for charitable giving or any similar tax benefit, in any jurisdiction, with respect to the Shared Amount paid to the Non-Profit Organisation; and (C) the Issuer will not independently verify that any Shared Amount has been or will 